WEBVTT

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.320
This is Shin Kazama, zero-zero section.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.020
This is Mickey Simon, blue section.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.820
Shin, what's up?

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.310
Enemy sighted at 12 o'clock.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.330
I see them.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.700
Judging by the speed, it looks like
they're MiG-21s.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.860
Maybe about thirty of 'em.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.270
Zero-zero section will provide
backup air support.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.100
Mickey, I'll leave the vanguard to you.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.480
AREA 88

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.950
Katamuku aozora
<i>A waning blue sky</i>
AREA 88

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.620
<i>A waning blue sky</i>
Katamuku aozora

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:33.320
BURNING MIRAGE

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:38.450
Honoo no mirage
<i>A mirage of flames</i>
BURNING MIRAGE

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:44.700
Inochi no ame wo wasureta
<i>A desert-like soul</i>

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.740
Sabaku no you na tamashii
<i>That has forgotten the rain of life</i>

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:55.640
Kimi wa doko e to yuku no ka
<i>Where are you going?</i>

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:01.850
Dare no tame naze tatakau
<i>Who are you fighting for and why?</i>

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.720
No one knows your pain of love
<i>No one knows your pain of love</i>

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.990
No one knows your loneliness
<i>No one knows your loneliness</i>

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:12.530
Atsui kaze ga kako kara fuite mo
<i>It's sad to see you walking away</i>

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.930
Atsui kaze ga kako kara fuite mo
<i>Unable to turn back</i>

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:21.180
Furimukenai senaka ga kanashii
<i>Even when a hot wind blows from the past</i>

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:41.790
All units proceed to locate enemy craft.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.850
Fire your sparrows and then reverse course.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.160
Range on... Fire!

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.700
Here comes a quick 4,000 bucks.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.450
Zero-zero section: all units storm the enemy.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.710
Attack!

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:40.040
All right, here I go...

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.910
Time to test the capabilities of this F-20
Tigershark I bought with all the money I had!

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.510
You've noticed me too late.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.720
That's Jess from zero-zero section.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.980
Shin! I've got a bandit on my six!

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:01.310
Jess!

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.150
They got me, Shin!

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.120
I... I can't see!

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.390
Eject!

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.550
Drop speed and pull down the handles
on your face curtain!

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.230
It's no use! The egress mechanism's shot!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.430
I forgot to get it repaired!

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.450
They shot me!

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:36.940
You son of a bitch!

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:43.730
Stop it, Jess!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:44.890
I shot down the bandit!

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:46.760
I'll guide you down, so hold down on your stick!

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:48.300
Now level your plane!

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.130
I can't tell, Shin!

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:52.600
Which way's up? Which way's down?

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:55.270
What kind of path am I flying right now?!

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:59.140
All I know is that I'm scared outta my mind!

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.170
Here's another one!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.080
Stop it! That's one of our Phantoms!

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:14.220
God dammit! I can't see it!
I don't know if it's friend or foe!

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:19.420
Get a hold of yourself, Jess!
Listen to me carefully!

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:28.470
Damn it, do something, Shin! I can't
keep my cool and fight like this!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.810
No way am I going to lose my money

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:34.070
because I took 30mm rounds up the ass
from one of my own men before I got it!

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:42.950
Jess...

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:49.290
You weren't lucky today.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:41.940
Man, oh, man...

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.710
The anti-government forces have been
putting up a fight lately.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:49.380
No matter how many times we beat 'em down,
they just keep on adding to their forces.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.490
For cryin' out loud, what the hell's
going on here anyway?!

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:28.990
You see something out there?

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.720
Nope, just a mirage.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.970
What were you thinking about?

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:52.550
I was wondering when it was that I stopped
feeling anything when I kill.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.550
This about Jess?

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:02.790
You did it to protect a large number of your
allies. You didn't have any choice, now did you?

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.730
If it had been my section, then I would
have taken care of him.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:07.500
It's not just Jess.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:10.430
I have to kill to earn that 1.5 million dollars,

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:14.770
but if I need to buy a new plane, then I have to
shoot down even more of the enemy.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.240
And for what?

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.140
So I can get out of here.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:21.010
In order to escape to a life where
I don't have to kill,

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.770
I stain my hands with blood murdering people.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.780
And even despite the fact that I'm doing
such a terrible thing,

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.840
somewhere along the line I stopped
feeling anything about it.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:32.320
I wonder when that was?

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:34.020
You're filthy, all filthy.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:38.960
You're completely soiled by the
grime of war, just like me.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.050
And it don't wash off either.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:52.110
I've gotta say this is a surprise!

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:55.540
I was all freaked out, wondering what kind of
man this Shin Kazama, Area 88's top killer,

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:59.480
the supposed king of the skies I've
heard so much about, really is.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:06.450
I never expected he'd be such a sappy little kid.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.390
You're new here, aren't you?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:15.100
Nguyen Van Chom, former first lieutenant
in the South Vietnamese air force.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.170
I just got here today.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.500
Yeah, Commander Saki and I...

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:25.870
We said our hellos just a little while ago.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:31.910
By the way, there's something I wanna ask you.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:32.810
How should I put it?

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:36.810
Around here do you, uh, get paid even for
shooting down your comrades?

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:39.120
You see...

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:42.060
I'm also used to seein' blood myself,

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:45.690
but if I'm gonna have to be careful
even of my own rear guard,

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:48.250
I figure that I'll really have
my work cut out for me.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.710
Why do we fight?

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:07.620
Why do we kill?

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.880
To survive!

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:15.090
Listen, Nguyen. I fight to survive.

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:18.060
Are you telling me I'm supposed to draw a line
between friend and foe in a fight for survival?

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.260
If you don't want to be killed by me,

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:23.030
then don't get in my way.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.960
Ooh, I'm shakin' now!

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.000
I think we're going to get along real well,
Shin Kazama.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.320
Christ, another asshole has signed on.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.150
Do you know him?

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:48.260
He's known as the Man-Eating Tiger
of the Gulf of Tonkin.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.780
In Vietnam, he's famous in a small way.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.750
Well, how about that.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.970
Ah, so there you are.

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:01.230
I've been looking for you two.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:05.470
Here, it's your invoice for this month.

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:06.940
Aw, man!

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:09.710
$20,000?!

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:11.880
Isn't that a little steep?!

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:15.180
If $20,000 will save your life,
I'd say that's a sweet deal.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:16.650
Exactly.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:18.950
You owe $50,000, Mickey.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:24.360
Hey, Pops, there must be some mistake here!

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:28.630
Those Tomcats are insanely big, and they
swallow up funds like nobody's business.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.760
Now that hurts!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.940
Oh, that's right, Shin.

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:37.540
You said you used to work for
Yamato Airlines, right?

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:38.940
Yeah...

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.340
What about it?

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:44.750
I heard this from a West German trader, but he
was saying that company's in big trouble.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.910
In trouble?

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:48.820
What do you mean?

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.990
It sounds like they've replaced
their company president.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.560
I hear they consequently replaced a bunch
of their equipment suppliers.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:57.330
Is that true?!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:02.300
There's a single company by the name of
Maxwell handling all of their new parts now,

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:05.470
but I hear they also supply a huge
amount of weaponry to the East.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:10.510
It's rumored that these arms are making it into
the hands of Aslan's rebel army, among others.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.910
Who's the new president?

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.810
Hmm... Now, what was his name?

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.780
Oh, those Japanese names are
so hard to remember...

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:21.320
Uh... Ka, ka, kan...

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:21.980
Um, Kanza...

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:22.150
Kanzaki!
Um, Kanza...

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:22.740
Kanzaki!

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:26.690
Yeah, that's it! Kanzaki!

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:27.720
Huh?

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.550
You mean you know him, Shin?

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:32.590
Kanzaki? How did he ever...

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:34.830
Well, that's the story.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:35.700
Wait a minute, old man!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.700
Whoa, Shin! Don't be so rough!

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:41.600
I'm just a weak old man!

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.840
Give me more details, McCoy!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.340
What's gotten into you, Shin?

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:49.340
What's become of the previous president?
What about his family?!

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.750
Don't be unreasonable!

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:54.770
This is all stuff that's happening far away in
another country! How am I supposed to know?

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.590
Listen, old man. I'll pay you whatever it takes.

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:02.560
Please find out more about Yamato Airlines!

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:06.290
Shin, what in the world is going on here?

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:07.230
Please!

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:09.860
You're the one who could dig up information
even from the Kremlin,

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:11.230
provided you had the funds, right?

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:13.100
All right, all right.

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:16.100
I'll be going to West Germany next week
to talk some business,

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.130
so I'll look into it for you then.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.770
The company president's chair isn't bad at all.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:55.380
Sir, Ryoko Tsugumo is here to see you.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.280
Ryoko?

00:16:57.280 --> 00:16:59.870
Instead of here, please see her
into the reception...

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:09.460
Ryoko...

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.660
The president's chair suits you well, doesn't it?

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:16.160
Well, you got me!

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:18.670
Why don't we go to the reception room?

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:20.370
Right here will be fine.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:24.740
I wanted to see you in your element now
that you're company president.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:31.650
How is your father doing?

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.050
I think it was quite a shock to him

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:36.880
when his seat was usurped at the
general stockholders' meeting.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:45.130
He's had a heart condition for some time,
so I was extremely worried about him.

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:48.030
But his condition finally began to improve,
so he is in Paris now.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.570
Glad to hear it.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:52.330
So, what brings you here today?

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:53.600
Ah, yes...

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:58.000
Actually...

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:07.780
These are...

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:10.350
Stock certificates totaling 120 million yen.

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:15.190
We've managed to scrape together another 180
million by liquidating all of our other assets.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:18.020
Don't tell me you plan to get rid of this stock!

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.530
I reached my decision after talking
about it with my father.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:22.790
We absolutely must have 300 million yen.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:25.330
What on Earth for?

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:29.030
Tell me, Ryoko!

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:33.070
He... Right now, he is in a
foreign legion in Aslan.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:36.040
If we pay off a penalty sum,
he can retire from service!

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:40.480
You're doing this for Shin?

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:45.450
But this is all the property you
and your father have.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:47.090
If you lose these...

00:18:47.090 --> 00:18:50.320
We can bear any burden if it's for his sake!

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.460
Please!

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:04.330
Any burden, you say?

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:08.780
Very well.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:12.710
You'd probably get less than 80 million
for them on the market.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.770
But I'll buy them from you at a premium.

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:16.820
I'm grateful.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:16.950
However...
I'm grateful.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:17.540
However...

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:19.520
There is one condition.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:34.370
I'd like you to keep me company tonight.

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:39.740
You said just now that you could
bear anything for him. Right?

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:51.090
I can see it was a mistake to come to you.

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:53.350
I'll sell this stock on my own, you'll see!

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:54.820
Fine by me.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.620
Sell your heart out.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:20:00.260
But you're no longer daughter of the
president of Yamato Airlines.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:03.760
You're the daughter of a pitiful man who's
been kicked out of his own company.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:07.130
I wonder how well people out there
are going to trust you?

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:13.710
Oh, you'll be back.

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:16.200
Yeah, you can count on it.

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:41.570
Easy, there, easy! Be careful with that thing!

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:44.710
If there's so much as a scratch on it,
I'll take the damages out of your pay, got it?!

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.370
Welcome back, old McCoy.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:49.280
Ah, Shin! You're still alive, huh?

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:52.300
Hey! What part of "be careful" don't
you understand, you jerks?!

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:59.320
The Maxwell Corporation has
a pretty bad reputation.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:02.160
They've supposedly taken over a large
number of foreign companies,

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:04.430
using the same kinds of tactics every time.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:06.660
They use shareholders with inside connections

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.400
to buy up shares of the company
they're targeting,

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:11.230
and they do it in a very clever manner.

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:14.500
They never have any single shareholder
buy more than three percent at most.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:17.140
But it's all planned so that just before
the next shareholders' meeting,

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:21.210
a certain individual winds up with
all of the shares they collected.

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:25.280
If they control forty percent of a company's
holdings, that company's in the bag.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:26.510
I see...

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:31.390
So Maxwell set their sights on Kanzaki, since
they didn't have any agencies in Japan, huh?

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:32.390
You got it.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:35.120
However, no names are ever
released to the public.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:39.420
Officially, the company president suddenly gets
replaced. Nothing more, nothing less.

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:46.000
And the Maxwell Corporation just introduced the
next-generation Airbus model, the MB-14.

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.670
They seem pretty pleased with themselves

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:49.800
for bringing out a plane that's so cheap and
that can carry so many passengers.

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:57.440
They say Yamato Airlines has been using it
for Southeast Asian and European flights,

00:21:57.440 --> 00:21:59.850
and they've been making money hand over fist.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.050
Well, isn't that grand?

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.850
If you take the news at face value,

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:08.950
pretty soon you'll be seeing MB-14s
flying all over the world.

00:22:09.860 --> 00:22:11.060
Isn't that the case?

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:14.550
It's their cheapness that rubs
me the wrong way.

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:19.890
What I heard from a West German merchant
is that the MB-14s have a lot of defects.

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:23.300
Their engines overheat very easily,

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:26.640
and there are questions regarding the durability
of a lot of the other components as well.

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:30.610
Sure, it's passed the tests for
a passenger aircraft,

00:22:30.610 --> 00:22:34.280
but well, it just barely reaches the
minimum standards, I'd bet.

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:38.050
It'll probably take a few accidents
for them to get it.

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:51.200
And a disaster like that will only bring
their company more trouble

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:54.970
'cuz it'll be five hundred or more of their own
passengers going up in flames.

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:59.870
This Kanzaki guy is walking one
hell of a tightrope, isn't he?

00:23:01.010 --> 00:23:03.780
Tell me, old man, what about the
former director and his family?

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:06.410
They said he's receiving medical
treatment in Paris.

00:23:06.410 --> 00:23:09.620
Except his daughter is supposedly still in Tokyo.

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:12.450
She probably plans to go back to her
father soon enough, I'm sure.

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:19.020
Oh yeah, here's the address and phone number
of the apartment the guy is renting in Paris.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:24.030
Just so you know, it cost me a lot of
money to get that information.

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:25.620
All right.

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:27.700
How much?

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:30.070
Hey, forget about it!

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:33.540
You're one of my best customers after all.
It's on me.

00:23:33.540 --> 00:23:35.770
Oh, that's right...

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.110
I brought you back a souvenir.

00:23:38.110 --> 00:23:41.550
Found it in a Japanese market in Frankfurt.

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:44.520
Check it out.

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:45.990
Cup ramen!

00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:48.320
They said you'll need these too.

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:50.890
That's pretty thoughtful of you!

00:23:50.890 --> 00:23:54.830
Listen, Shin. That's the kind of company
Yamato Airlines is.

00:23:54.830 --> 00:23:56.360
Just forget about it.

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:57.800
Old man...

00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:00.030
I don't know what happened before,

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:02.370
but you're better off not worrying
about other people's fates.

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:04.540
This is Area 88.

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:07.470
It's a fierce war zone, the absolute
lowest point of Hell.

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:10.140
If you let yourself get weighed down
by unneeded burdens,

00:24:10.140 --> 00:24:11.880
it can make you start shaking
when you grip your stick

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:14.620
and dull your ability to make
split-second decisions.

00:24:14.620 --> 00:24:17.690
I've encountered a lot of men
like that, understand?

00:24:17.690 --> 00:24:19.240
Yeah...

00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:20.820
Well, see ya.

00:24:20.820 --> 00:24:23.120
Enjoy your long-awaited little
taste of Japan there.

00:24:26.530 --> 00:24:28.720
Thanks, old McCoy.

00:24:38.510 --> 00:24:43.910
"This Kanzaki guy is walking one
hell of a tightrope, isn't he?"

00:24:44.610 --> 00:24:46.250
Kanzaki...

00:24:46.250 --> 00:24:48.740
Is that what your dream was?

00:24:49.320 --> 00:24:52.420
What about your dream from way back, when we
used to talk about flying the skies together?

00:24:52.420 --> 00:24:54.580
Was it a lie?

00:24:55.620 --> 00:24:57.890
Answer me, Kanzaki!

00:25:21.420 --> 00:25:23.650
Gotta wait three minutes after pouring
in the hot water, right?

00:25:47.540 --> 00:25:49.110
Good afternoon!

00:25:49.110 --> 00:25:50.270
Huh?

00:25:51.710 --> 00:25:53.480
Oh, Ms. Yasuda.

00:25:54.250 --> 00:25:57.450
Dear me, you haven't even
put away your things?

00:25:57.890 --> 00:26:01.190
It's no big deal. After all, I won't
be here for very long.

00:26:02.190 --> 00:26:04.820
How did it go with Mr. Kanzaki?

00:26:07.660 --> 00:26:10.300
It's like I only went there to have
him make a fool of me.

00:26:10.300 --> 00:26:13.200
He was never someone I could
count on for help.

00:26:15.400 --> 00:26:17.300
Oh, I almost forgot...

00:26:17.300 --> 00:26:21.540
Miss Tsugumo, I tried reexamining
a few account ledgers,

00:26:21.540 --> 00:26:24.040
but that man, Kanzaki, really
is something else! He...

00:26:24.040 --> 00:26:25.380
Huh?

00:26:25.380 --> 00:26:26.910
Miss Tsugumo...

00:26:26.910 --> 00:26:28.680
What's that smell?

00:26:30.020 --> 00:26:31.420
Oh, no!

00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:35.260
Aw, I knew it.

00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:37.390
They've turned to complete mush!

00:26:37.390 --> 00:26:39.720
Oh, Miss...

00:26:51.970 --> 00:26:55.510
ATC, ATC... This is Yamato Airlines Flight 31.

00:26:55.510 --> 00:26:57.340
We are currently en route to Osaka.

00:26:57.340 --> 00:27:00.180
Presently 38 kilometers west of Ooshima.

00:27:00.180 --> 00:27:02.950
Request descend FL 220 from 240.

00:27:02.950 --> 00:27:05.850
This is Tokyo Air Traffic Control.

00:27:05.850 --> 00:27:06.790
Proceed.

00:27:10.090 --> 00:27:13.790
First, put the life jacket over your head.

00:27:13.790 --> 00:27:17.460
Next, attach the metal fittings on both sides
to the front fasteners on your vest,

00:27:17.460 --> 00:27:19.260
and tighten by pulling on the straps.

00:27:24.670 --> 00:27:26.810
Fire alert for engine one!

00:27:26.810 --> 00:27:28.370
Shut down engine one!

00:27:32.080 --> 00:27:34.740
Engine one, automatic fire extinguisher
is not functioning!

00:27:37.220 --> 00:27:39.490
Engine three, output falling.

00:27:39.490 --> 00:27:40.980
It's caught fire!

00:27:54.970 --> 00:27:58.140
ATC! ATC! This is Yamato Airlines Flight 31!

00:27:58.140 --> 00:28:00.700
Mayday! Mayday!

00:28:03.110 --> 00:28:05.680
I'm receiving an emergency call
from Yamato Flight 31!

00:28:05.680 --> 00:28:07.980
Yamato 31, are you returning to Haneda?!

00:28:07.980 --> 00:28:10.380
Engine fire! Power output falling!

00:28:10.380 --> 00:28:12.880
Unable to control! Unable to control!

00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:25.030
Was this accident due to pilot error?

00:28:25.030 --> 00:28:27.900
We've been told that the engines caught fire,
but what caused this?

00:28:28.370 --> 00:28:31.370
We have not yet completed our
investigation of the accident.

00:28:31.370 --> 00:28:33.910
Until the flight data recorder and cockpit
voice recorder are recovered,

00:28:33.910 --> 00:28:35.340
we won't be able to give any details.

00:28:35.680 --> 00:28:40.550
One hundred fifty dead have been confirmed
so far, but what of survivors?

00:28:40.550 --> 00:28:43.380
There is still no word of any survivors.

00:28:43.380 --> 00:28:45.420
How do you plan to apologize
to the victims' families?

00:28:45.420 --> 00:28:47.320
Who will take responsibility?

00:28:47.320 --> 00:28:50.350
We intend to do all that we possibly can.

00:28:50.820 --> 00:28:54.260
We've heard that all MB-14s
have been grounded.

00:28:54.260 --> 00:28:55.260
Why is that?

00:28:55.260 --> 00:28:56.900
Just so we can be on the safe side,

00:28:56.900 --> 00:28:59.000
I've ordered all of them to be reinspected
and serviced, that's all.

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:01.370
Then you acknowledge the rumors?

00:29:01.370 --> 00:29:02.170
Rumors?

00:29:02.170 --> 00:29:06.570
The rumors that the Maxwell MB-14
is defect-prone.

00:29:06.570 --> 00:29:07.940
That is ridiculous!

00:29:07.940 --> 00:29:11.350
A faulty aircraft would never be able
to qualify as a passenger plane!

00:29:11.350 --> 00:29:15.780
But there are accounts of earlier
problems with the MB-14, and...

00:29:15.780 --> 00:29:18.220
Hey, where are you going?
Aren't you going to answer me?!

00:29:19.390 --> 00:29:21.890
It did have engine trouble though, didn't it?

00:29:21.890 --> 00:29:25.290
As I told you before, we do not know
what caused the accident.

00:29:25.290 --> 00:29:28.060
In any event, the accident investigation
commission will present its findings, won't it?

00:29:28.060 --> 00:29:29.860
I ask you to please not write based
solely off of speculation!

00:29:29.860 --> 00:29:30.630
Hey!

00:29:30.630 --> 00:29:31.000
Wait!
Hey!

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:31.770
Wait!
What the heck kind of press conference is this?!

00:29:31.770 --> 00:29:32.560
What the heck kind of press conference is this?!

00:29:37.700 --> 00:29:40.870
Are you sure grounding all those flights
wasn't a bad idea after all?

00:29:40.870 --> 00:29:42.970
Now it looks like we're acknowledging
the rumors.

00:29:43.080 --> 00:29:45.380
And what would you do if there
was another disaster?

00:29:45.380 --> 00:29:47.180
The fact is that plane had engine problems.

00:29:47.180 --> 00:29:49.420
Damn it... Who let that out?

00:29:49.420 --> 00:29:52.150
This means we'll have to perform
a thorough check of the aircraft

00:29:52.150 --> 00:29:53.920
to prove that they are not defective.

00:29:53.920 --> 00:29:55.090
Where are the victims' remains?

00:29:55.090 --> 00:29:56.260
At Domyo Temple.

00:29:56.260 --> 00:29:58.630
But you're scheduled to meet the representative
of the accident investigation commission...

00:29:58.630 --> 00:30:00.030
Domyo Temple comes first!

00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:02.760
As for the commission representative...
You're the managing director; you deal with him.

00:30:09.300 --> 00:30:11.970
With our insurance we can manage to cover
consolation payments to the victims' families,

00:30:11.970 --> 00:30:14.510
but what about confidence in our company?

00:30:14.510 --> 00:30:17.940
We knew the MB-14 only barely met
the minimum standards for safety,

00:30:17.940 --> 00:30:19.250
and so it was that much cheaper.

00:30:19.250 --> 00:30:20.310
But even still,

00:30:20.310 --> 00:30:23.580
only six months into active service, and already
we have an accident? What the hell is that?!

00:30:23.580 --> 00:30:26.650
Anyway, I want to meet with you
in London soon. Next week.

00:30:26.650 --> 00:30:27.920
What?!

00:30:30.220 --> 00:30:32.530
Hey! That's not going to work for me!

00:30:32.530 --> 00:30:34.930
It's not just our company, you know.
People will also lose faith in your...

00:30:35.760 --> 00:30:37.320
Dammit...

00:30:37.600 --> 00:30:39.070
What did they say at Maxwell?

00:30:39.070 --> 00:30:41.940
He asked me to postpone our meeting.

00:30:41.940 --> 00:30:44.200
It's obvious that they're just
trying to buy some time

00:30:44.200 --> 00:30:46.440
to try and figure out a way to get
themselves out of this mess.

00:30:46.440 --> 00:30:50.510
If they're forced against the wall, they'll
just abandon Yamato Airlines.

00:30:50.510 --> 00:30:51.880
That's just the kind of guys they are.

00:30:51.880 --> 00:30:55.470
Damn it all... So you intend to sacrifice
me to save yourselves?!

00:31:35.490 --> 00:31:36.960
Sir!

00:31:47.730 --> 00:31:49.240
What a disaster...

00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:52.340
But it's not going to trip me up!

00:31:52.340 --> 00:31:54.430
I'm not going to be beaten by this!

00:32:04.850 --> 00:32:08.190
The enemy's fuel stores are located at this point.

00:32:08.190 --> 00:32:11.160
The rebel forces have become aggressive
lately in their advance.

00:32:11.160 --> 00:32:14.930
If we can destroy this, we'll be able to immobilize
them for at least three months.

00:32:14.930 --> 00:32:16.300
Wait a second, Saki!

00:32:16.300 --> 00:32:19.570
The government ground forces are just
a hundred miles ahead of us.

00:32:19.570 --> 00:32:23.170
The ground forces should have some
helicopters or light aircraft.

00:32:23.170 --> 00:32:26.270
I don't get why they're passing
the job along to us!

00:32:26.270 --> 00:32:31.140
It's like this: the mission's beneath
the regular army's level.

00:32:31.140 --> 00:32:36.520
What's that all about? So what kind of
level does that put us at?

00:32:36.520 --> 00:32:40.480
When there's a high likelihood there'll be
casualties, they pass the job on to us.

00:32:41.050 --> 00:32:43.290
Am I right, Commander Saki?

00:32:43.290 --> 00:32:47.020
You're all étrangers who came here
with full knowledge of that fact.

00:32:47.330 --> 00:32:51.000
The problem is this ravine. It's so big
you could call it a crevasse.

00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:53.800
It's 400 meters wide, and 500 meters deep.

00:32:53.800 --> 00:32:57.770
It runs a total of almost 500 kilometers,
meandering along in an S-shaped curve.

00:32:57.770 --> 00:33:00.710
Ah, now I get it.
The ground forces can't cross it.

00:33:00.710 --> 00:33:03.680
And the enemy probably has radar
covering the airspace above it,

00:33:03.680 --> 00:33:07.310
so army choppers or light aircraft would end up
being shot down by enemy interceptors

00:33:07.310 --> 00:33:10.020
who'd take it as an opportunity
for a training exercise.

00:33:10.020 --> 00:33:11.320
You've got it.

00:33:11.320 --> 00:33:14.820
Of all the regular army's choppers and aircraft
which have staged attacks on the area so far,

00:33:14.820 --> 00:33:17.320
not a single one has made it
through to the target.

00:33:17.320 --> 00:33:21.190
To the enemy, this ravine is a
perfect natural defense.

00:33:21.190 --> 00:33:24.900
But depending on your point of view,
it could also be the ultimate vulnerability.

00:33:24.900 --> 00:33:26.200
Vulnerability?

00:33:26.200 --> 00:33:27.500
What's that supposed to mean?

00:33:27.500 --> 00:33:31.570
If we fly through this ravine, there is no way
we will be picked up on radar.

00:33:31.570 --> 00:33:32.970
I get it!

00:33:32.970 --> 00:33:34.500
Good idea!

00:33:35.240 --> 00:33:37.140
This is a cross-section of the ravine.

00:33:37.140 --> 00:33:39.680
The ravine's aperture is 400 meters,

00:33:39.680 --> 00:33:42.620
but it's not even 10 meters wide at the bottom,
which gives it a V-shaped cross section.

00:33:43.120 --> 00:33:44.680
There are five major sticking points.

00:33:45.020 --> 00:33:47.950
The terrain poses a greater problem
than the air currents.

00:33:47.950 --> 00:33:51.390
Even though it is a V-shape, there are a
number of large rock outcroppings.

00:33:55.900 --> 00:33:57.590
There's no way this will work!

00:33:58.300 --> 00:33:59.870
It's not like we can fly through that!

00:33:59.870 --> 00:34:01.400
Even a bird would get caught on those rocks!

00:34:01.400 --> 00:34:04.800
What idiot said this was a good idea, huh?!

00:34:04.800 --> 00:34:06.770
It was you, Campbell.

00:34:06.770 --> 00:34:09.410
If we pull up to avoid the rocks,
we get picked up by radar.

00:34:09.410 --> 00:34:11.210
If we fly too low, we crash on them.

00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:12.550
Forget that!

00:34:12.550 --> 00:34:14.710
I don't care how much this mission
might be at our "level."

00:34:14.710 --> 00:34:17.350
If we go out there, there's a hundred
percent chance we'll end up dead!

00:34:17.350 --> 00:34:19.750
That's what I thought too.

00:34:19.750 --> 00:34:21.350
But have a look at this.

00:34:22.120 --> 00:34:25.220
If I stack up the five cross sections...

00:34:25.790 --> 00:34:27.190
What about it?

00:34:27.190 --> 00:34:29.190
Don't you get it?

00:34:35.740 --> 00:34:39.070
About 250 meters below surface level,

00:34:39.070 --> 00:34:43.340
you have a tunnel about 25 meters wide
and 15 meters high.

00:34:43.340 --> 00:34:45.310
And are we going to fly through that?

00:34:45.310 --> 00:34:46.580
It'll be a close shave.

00:34:46.580 --> 00:34:49.620
Make the slightest mistake, and you'll
hit a rock and get broken to bits.

00:34:49.620 --> 00:34:51.890
But it's nothing we can't do.

00:34:51.890 --> 00:34:54.890
Just so long as we make damn sure to hold our
altitudes and positions perfectly steady.

00:34:54.890 --> 00:34:57.160
That's one extremely dangerous
tightrope though.

00:34:57.160 --> 00:34:59.460
We'll carry out the mission tonight.

00:34:59.460 --> 00:35:00.790
Tonight?!

00:35:00.790 --> 00:35:02.160
Man, that's nuts!

00:35:02.160 --> 00:35:04.000
As if it weren't already dangerous
enough to try in the daylight!

00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:07.400
That's exactly what puts this
mission at your level.

00:35:07.400 --> 00:35:10.300
You'll be paid very handsomely.
Three times the normal rate.

00:35:10.300 --> 00:35:14.600
And I don't mind if the survivors split the
earnings of those who do not return.

00:35:15.080 --> 00:35:16.740
Pretty frightening terms!

00:35:16.740 --> 00:35:19.740
'Cuz we've got some guys here who'll
go after their own allies!

00:35:36.300 --> 00:35:40.670
Jee-zus! Check out that asshole's gaudy
looking bomber, Shin!

00:35:44.670 --> 00:35:47.770
You mean that F-105 Thunderchief?

00:35:47.770 --> 00:35:49.580
You don't see too many of those these days.

00:35:49.580 --> 00:35:52.710
The US Air Force retired those from frontline
combat a long time ago, didn't they?

00:35:53.510 --> 00:35:54.880
How nice of you.

00:35:54.880 --> 00:35:56.380
But even so, these are bloodthirsty planes,

00:35:56.380 --> 00:35:59.080
and they saw a lot of service
in the skies over Vietnam!

00:36:11.870 --> 00:36:14.100
All units, correct your altimeters
to zero at target altitude!

00:36:17.840 --> 00:36:19.970
Time to walk the tightrope!

00:37:06.690 --> 00:37:08.380
Now approaching point one!

00:37:08.990 --> 00:37:10.460
Maintain altitude at zero!

00:37:10.460 --> 00:37:13.590
Five meters above or below zero is
the maximum permissible limit.

00:37:32.580 --> 00:37:37.350
Damn! Can't get any speed with all this
heavy equipment weighin' me down!

00:37:55.840 --> 00:37:57.060
Oaf!

00:38:02.680 --> 00:38:04.340
Now approaching point two!

00:38:08.880 --> 00:38:10.580
And coming up on point three!

00:38:10.580 --> 00:38:13.250
Bank left after you pass through,
and maintain altitude!

00:38:21.590 --> 00:38:23.560
Now approaching point four!

00:38:23.760 --> 00:38:25.430
Leonhardt! You're too low!

00:38:25.770 --> 00:38:27.130
Roger!

00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:42.750
This is the final point!

00:38:42.750 --> 00:38:45.780
After we pass through, we'll get in formation
and launch the attack all at once!

00:39:19.120 --> 00:39:22.620
Bomber squadron, maintain course, charge in
and drop your bombs over their fuel stores.

00:39:22.620 --> 00:39:24.720
Attack squadron, provide coverage
from the left flank.

00:39:24.720 --> 00:39:27.060
After that, you can do as you like while
you're counting your money!

00:39:27.060 --> 00:39:28.290
Attack!

00:39:49.350 --> 00:39:50.370
What's going on?!

00:39:52.850 --> 00:39:54.340
How the hell...

00:39:54.590 --> 00:39:56.690
Shin! We've flown into a trap!

00:39:56.690 --> 00:39:58.260
We're surrounded!

00:39:58.260 --> 00:39:59.990
Change course and engage the enemy fighters!

00:39:59.990 --> 00:40:02.360
We've already started our bombing approach.

00:40:02.360 --> 00:40:04.700
We can't just up and change course like that!

00:40:05.200 --> 00:40:06.460
We'll cover you!

00:40:25.250 --> 00:40:27.450
No wonder my ass itches!

00:40:27.450 --> 00:40:30.320
I've got a bunch of Harrier AV8As on it!

00:40:30.960 --> 00:40:33.290
What are the rebels doing with Western aircraft?!

00:40:33.690 --> 00:40:35.030
Hell if I know.

00:40:35.030 --> 00:40:38.360
All I can say is that these guys are
gonna give us some trouble.

00:40:38.870 --> 00:40:41.300
Protecting the bomber squadron is our priority.
Take them out!

00:41:21.870 --> 00:41:23.010
Shin!

00:41:23.010 --> 00:41:24.680
Move in towards the target!

00:41:24.680 --> 00:41:26.480
We've got this place covered!

00:41:58.380 --> 00:42:00.010
I've got you...

00:42:01.450 --> 00:42:02.880
He's gone!

00:42:43.020 --> 00:42:44.620
Harriers are good at pulling tight turns.

00:42:44.620 --> 00:42:47.330
It will cost you your life if you rely too
much on your computer, guys!

00:42:47.330 --> 00:42:50.520
All you can rely on here is the étranger's
intuition forged in the heat of battle!

00:42:52.500 --> 00:42:54.830
All right, will he jump up?

00:42:54.830 --> 00:42:55.930
No! He's going low!

00:43:08.410 --> 00:43:11.010
That's that. It's like playing a video game!

00:43:14.790 --> 00:43:17.760
Here they are! The ducks are all
lined up in a row!

00:43:21.730 --> 00:43:23.100
Just watch!

00:43:23.100 --> 00:43:27.060
I might not be as nimble as you, but I'll
show you how very much faster I am!

00:43:29.640 --> 00:43:33.730
Wait right there. I'll send every single
one of you to the next life!

00:43:50.990 --> 00:43:53.490
Spill, spill red blood all over!

00:43:53.490 --> 00:43:56.730
Let it gush out and paint my canopy red!

00:44:33.930 --> 00:44:35.960
You're not getting away.

00:44:36.300 --> 00:44:37.740
Nguyen! Stop!

00:45:07.270 --> 00:45:10.830
Moshimo shindara nonde kure yo
<i>If I die, please drink for me</i>

00:45:13.310 --> 00:45:16.870
Tsuyoi sake wo mizu mitai ni sa
<i>Put away strong booze like water</i>

00:45:19.010 --> 00:45:25.320
Shinpai suru na yo jigoku de harau sa
<i>Don't worry, I'll pay the bill in Hell</i>

00:45:25.650 --> 00:45:30.020
Ano hito ni wa shirasenakute ii
<i>You don't have to tell her about me</i>

00:45:31.590 --> 00:45:36.030
Ima wa chigau dare ka no mono sa
<i>I'm sure she belongs to someone else now</i>

00:45:37.960 --> 00:45:44.070
Dogfight, nido to sora wo tobenai
<i>Dogfight, I'll never be able to fly the skies again</i>

00:45:44.070 --> 00:45:47.140
<i>Dogfight, that's the only thing about this</i>
Dogfight, soitsu dake ga sabishii

00:45:47.140 --> 00:45:49.800
<i>That makes me sad
Dogfight, soitsu dake ga sabishii</i>

00:45:49.940 --> 00:45:54.400
Makeinu wa ochiru dake, dogfight
<i>Losers crash, that's all, dogfight!</i>

00:45:55.820 --> 00:45:57.340
Woo-hoo!

00:46:00.720 --> 00:46:04.890
I know it ain't the right season, but here's
a little present from Santa Claus!

00:46:46.670 --> 00:46:48.330
Then what about the stocks?

00:46:48.330 --> 00:46:50.870
They said you won't get any more
than 80 million yen.

00:46:50.870 --> 00:46:53.210
I looks like Mr. Kanzaki knew that after all.

00:46:53.210 --> 00:46:55.300
Don't we have any other options?

00:46:58.610 --> 00:47:00.440
I see...

00:47:01.580 --> 00:47:04.950
Then I suppose I have no choice but
to ask for Mr. Kanzaki's help.

00:47:04.950 --> 00:47:06.190
You mustn't do that!

00:47:06.190 --> 00:47:09.720
He's the very man who teamed up with
Maxwell to take over Yamato Airlines!

00:47:09.720 --> 00:47:13.230
And that Maxwell company's plane
is what killed all those people!

00:47:13.230 --> 00:47:14.960
So what should I do then?!

00:47:14.960 --> 00:47:17.090
I'm still 40 million yen short!

00:47:23.700 --> 00:47:25.200
I'm sorry...

00:47:25.200 --> 00:47:27.710
Ms. Tsugumo, please wait a little longer.

00:47:27.710 --> 00:47:32.210
I'm looking into it for you now,
into his relationship with Maxwell.

00:47:32.210 --> 00:47:35.340
Depending on what the situation is, we
may even be able to file a lawsuit!

00:47:36.720 --> 00:47:38.680
And what would that lead to?

00:47:38.680 --> 00:47:42.050
Even as we speak, Shin is being made to fight.

00:47:42.050 --> 00:47:45.960
Even if he survives today, there's no guarantee
he'll make it through tomorrow.

00:47:46.330 --> 00:47:49.260
The only thing that can save Shin is money.

00:47:49.260 --> 00:47:51.790
I need 300 million yen, and
that's all there is to it.

00:48:07.180 --> 00:48:10.520
Welcome, Lieutenant Colonel Vashtar.
We've been waiting for you.

00:48:10.520 --> 00:48:13.290
Roundell, thank you for your
hospitality once again.

00:48:13.290 --> 00:48:15.250
This is Shin and Mickey.

00:48:15.690 --> 00:48:20.230
Shin has received combat training here,
so I believe you know him?

00:48:20.230 --> 00:48:21.360
I see.

00:48:21.360 --> 00:48:24.760
The fledgling from three years ago has
managed to survive to today, eh?

00:48:24.760 --> 00:48:27.330
The look in your eyes has changed
a little too, hasn't it?

00:48:27.330 --> 00:48:30.100
I'll be having a meeting with Roundell now.

00:48:30.100 --> 00:48:32.870
You can just relax for awhile.
Go into town or something.

00:48:32.870 --> 00:48:35.710
Whew! That's much appreciated! Right?

00:48:39.750 --> 00:48:41.880
So who's the old man anyway?

00:48:41.880 --> 00:48:44.080
He's in command of the combat training base.

00:48:44.080 --> 00:48:46.140
He put me through the wringer.

00:48:46.820 --> 00:48:48.150
Huh...

00:48:48.150 --> 00:48:50.890
So they teach you how to be
a killer here, do they?

00:48:51.090 --> 00:48:57.400
Yeah, those who only have civilian or
commercial licenses get their training here.

00:48:57.400 --> 00:49:00.700
Left, right, left, right, left, right...

00:49:00.700 --> 00:49:03.000
Oh, those guys?

00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:06.400
They're new recruits, like me three years ago.

00:49:11.740 --> 00:49:12.980
Oh, brother...

00:49:12.980 --> 00:49:14.780
Those guys are stupid, huh?

00:49:14.780 --> 00:49:17.180
Whatever made them come here
of their own free will?

00:49:17.180 --> 00:49:20.120
Civilian life's a helluva lot easier than this!

00:49:20.120 --> 00:49:23.720
It's too late. Just a single sheet
of paper takes you to Hell.

00:49:23.720 --> 00:49:25.420
Just a single sheet of paper...

00:49:25.420 --> 00:49:27.590
Sign it and you're whisked off to Hell.

00:49:27.590 --> 00:49:29.960
Concentrate on surviving...

00:49:38.070 --> 00:49:39.600
A Japanese!

00:49:43.280 --> 00:49:46.310
I wonder what Saki wants to talk
to the old guy about?

00:49:46.310 --> 00:49:47.750
Have you heard?

00:49:47.750 --> 00:49:51.220
Probably about having the Aslan capital's
defense force reinforced.

00:49:51.220 --> 00:49:54.290
At this rate, it's in danger, and no joke.

00:49:54.290 --> 00:49:57.260
Are you saying the rebel forces
will invade the capital?

00:49:57.260 --> 00:50:01.890
Both sides see the capital as sacred ground,
where they absolutely can't spill blood.

00:50:02.190 --> 00:50:05.000
Aslan is right between Eastern and
Western spheres of influence,

00:50:05.000 --> 00:50:07.600
so they're faced with a tricky situation.

00:50:07.600 --> 00:50:14.410
There are even individuals in the West who
scheme to profit here by disrupting this balance.

00:50:14.410 --> 00:50:16.410
The Harriers we fought before
are a good example.

00:50:16.410 --> 00:50:18.480
If these guys have got the merchants of death
spurring them on,

00:50:18.480 --> 00:50:20.980
you can be sure they'll launch a raid
even on the holy ground.

00:50:20.980 --> 00:50:23.380
The Maxwell Corporation...

00:50:23.380 --> 00:50:25.780
They caused a big accident over in Japan, huh?

00:50:25.780 --> 00:50:29.090
Then they dumped their Airbus as quick as they
could and started pushing their fighter jet sales.

00:50:29.090 --> 00:50:30.590
Talk about resilient...

00:50:30.590 --> 00:50:32.160
If something isn't done fast,

00:50:32.160 --> 00:50:35.360
this country will fall under the control of
merchants of death like those guys.

00:50:35.360 --> 00:50:37.360
So Saki's feeling the heat too.

00:50:37.360 --> 00:50:41.430
This is no time for his old man and uncle
to be fighting over the throne!

00:50:41.430 --> 00:50:44.200
Christ, what a messed-up family!

00:50:44.900 --> 00:50:47.810
Hey, not that I really care...

00:50:47.810 --> 00:50:50.010
But it's nothing but couples here!

00:50:50.010 --> 00:50:52.310
We're like the only two guys that
are hanging around together.

00:50:52.310 --> 00:50:54.580
That ain't right.

00:50:54.580 --> 00:50:55.780
What are you talking about?

00:50:55.780 --> 00:50:57.580
You're the one who suggested we come here.

00:50:57.880 --> 00:50:59.180
Excuse me!

00:50:59.180 --> 00:51:00.990
Would you mind taking our picture?

00:51:00.990 --> 00:51:03.420
Huh? Oh, right, sure thing.

00:51:04.060 --> 00:51:05.460
You see?

00:51:08.030 --> 00:51:09.830
Okay, say "peace!"

00:51:15.970 --> 00:51:18.060
Tracy!

00:51:26.150 --> 00:51:28.940
Sorry, but could you please hurry?

00:51:30.880 --> 00:51:32.080
Right...

00:51:39.220 --> 00:51:40.190
Thanks!

00:51:40.190 --> 00:51:42.750
Well, I just hope I got a good shot there.

00:51:43.360 --> 00:51:44.500
You two newlyweds?

00:51:44.500 --> 00:51:46.190
Yeah, kinda...

00:51:46.800 --> 00:51:49.030
Enjoy your lives together!

00:51:57.880 --> 00:51:59.970
Well, that sure caught me off-guard!

00:52:00.510 --> 00:52:02.780
Ran right into my old lover.

00:52:09.420 --> 00:52:11.750
Is that woman Tracy?

00:52:12.490 --> 00:52:14.890
They're on their honeymoon.

00:52:19.200 --> 00:52:22.170
I guess it serves me right!

00:52:28.570 --> 00:52:30.410
Say, Shin...

00:52:31.140 --> 00:52:36.380
I hope your lover back in Tokyo waits for you.

00:52:36.380 --> 00:52:38.210
Ryoko...

00:52:40.720 --> 00:52:42.650
She'll wait for me.

00:52:49.760 --> 00:52:53.270
A city that is like a tiny oasis
surrounded by a vast desert.

00:52:53.270 --> 00:52:55.200
In essence, that is Aslan.

00:52:55.200 --> 00:52:59.870
Though small, Aslan was a peaceful
and wealthy country.

00:52:59.870 --> 00:53:03.100
At least, until my mother died.

00:53:03.880 --> 00:53:06.480
My mother was loved by everyone.

00:53:06.480 --> 00:53:11.250
And she, in turn, loved this country
more than anyone else.

00:53:11.580 --> 00:53:14.250
The old king had two sons, you see.

00:53:14.250 --> 00:53:16.560
The older brother was my father, Abdael,

00:53:16.560 --> 00:53:20.060
and the younger brother was Zak,
the present king of Aslan.

00:53:20.060 --> 00:53:22.730
The previous king was a progressive,

00:53:22.730 --> 00:53:26.970
but despised his elder son, who sought
to draw in foreign capital.

00:53:26.970 --> 00:53:29.740
He handed the throne over to the younger
brother, who was a conservative.

00:53:29.740 --> 00:53:33.970
Naturally, my father, who had believed
that he would be the next king,

00:53:33.970 --> 00:53:36.610
started to hate his younger brother.

00:53:36.610 --> 00:53:41.570
Taking the eventual death of the king as his cue,
my father plotted an insurrection.

00:53:41.710 --> 00:53:46.850
Yes, he even proposed that I ally myself to his
cause. After all, we are father and son.

00:53:46.850 --> 00:53:49.590
However, for my mother's sake I refused.

00:53:49.590 --> 00:53:52.260
My father also loved my mother very deeply,

00:53:52.260 --> 00:53:59.290
and I was sure he would never defile the
soil in which she was laid to rest.

00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:02.600
Yet in the end, under the influence
of foreign industrialists,

00:54:02.600 --> 00:54:07.670
he established an anti-government
regiment and started a civil war.

00:54:08.810 --> 00:54:12.310
I suppose I've foisted a rather dull
story on you, haven't I?

00:54:12.310 --> 00:54:13.810
Not at all.

00:54:13.810 --> 00:54:17.020
Though it doesn't really have
anything to do with me.

00:54:17.020 --> 00:54:19.890
There's no point in talking to others
about one's own past,

00:54:19.890 --> 00:54:21.650
and it's impolite to ask someone
else about theirs.

00:54:21.650 --> 00:54:24.660
That's what a foreign legion is,
or so I've been taught.

00:54:24.660 --> 00:54:26.720
No doubt about that.

00:54:28.030 --> 00:54:32.690
It appears that returning to my birthplace after
so long has made me rather prone to grumbling.

00:54:33.000 --> 00:54:35.800
Even though there is such internal conflict,
this place is an oasis.

00:54:35.800 --> 00:54:40.270
People live here, tourists come to visit...
I'm sure a damp breeze blows through it too.

00:54:40.270 --> 00:54:44.870
This is an oasis, and Area 88 is in the middle of
a desert that will dry even your heart out.

00:54:56.820 --> 00:54:57.760
Shin!

00:54:58.920 --> 00:55:01.950
Shin, it's me! Wake up!

00:55:03.460 --> 00:55:04.500
What's the matter, Saki?

00:55:04.500 --> 00:55:05.730
A deserter.

00:55:05.730 --> 00:55:07.600
A deserter?

00:55:07.600 --> 00:55:10.400
Gimme a break. I'm under contract
with the foreign legion,

00:55:10.400 --> 00:55:11.600
but I'm not paramilitary personnel.

00:55:11.600 --> 00:55:13.970
Catching deserters is not my duty.

00:55:14.470 --> 00:55:16.880
Actually, we've already caught him.

00:55:16.880 --> 00:55:19.440
Shuichiro Ito, he's Japanese.

00:55:19.910 --> 00:55:21.250
Japanese?!

00:55:21.250 --> 00:55:23.880
He just enlisted today,

00:55:23.880 --> 00:55:27.950
but he has signed the enlistment form, so he'll
be treated as full-fledged military personnel.

00:55:27.950 --> 00:55:30.090
What will they do with him?

00:55:30.090 --> 00:55:32.860
He'll be executed by firing squad, the standard
punishment for a wartime deserter.

00:55:32.860 --> 00:55:34.260
Or so I imagine.

00:55:35.060 --> 00:55:36.660
By firing squad?

00:55:36.660 --> 00:55:39.570
He said that he would like to speak with you.

00:55:39.570 --> 00:55:45.100
It seems a soldier told him about the Japanese
ace pilot who's rampaging throughout Aslan.

00:55:45.100 --> 00:55:47.670
His court-martial will be held soon,

00:55:47.670 --> 00:55:49.910
but the trial will be over in just ten minutes.

00:55:49.910 --> 00:55:52.670
He'll be taken to the execution grounds
one hour after the end of the trial.

00:56:01.450 --> 00:56:03.720
You have ten minutes.

00:56:16.940 --> 00:56:19.870
You're Shin Kazama, right?

00:56:19.870 --> 00:56:21.810
They said you wanted a word with me.

00:56:21.810 --> 00:56:23.710
They say you're really something.

00:56:23.710 --> 00:56:26.010
The most famous fighter of Area 88!

00:56:28.980 --> 00:56:30.820
That was a stupid thing to do.

00:56:30.820 --> 00:56:33.690
You'd have been able to return home
to Japan in three years.

00:56:33.690 --> 00:56:37.210
After murdering person after person
for three years?

00:56:38.120 --> 00:56:40.160
I'd never be able to do it.

00:56:40.160 --> 00:56:42.960
I'd never be able to kill a man.

00:56:45.700 --> 00:56:48.870
So how many have you killed so far? Huh?

00:56:48.870 --> 00:56:50.240
Tell me, Mr. Kazama.

00:56:50.240 --> 00:56:52.170
It's kill or be killed!

00:56:52.170 --> 00:56:53.840
This isn't Japan!

00:56:53.840 --> 00:56:56.070
You think naïve pacifistic ideals
will hold water here?!

00:56:56.070 --> 00:56:58.310
It's about your life, your own!

00:56:58.310 --> 00:57:00.610
You're the only one who can protect it!

00:57:00.610 --> 00:57:02.750
That's right, it's my own life.

00:57:02.750 --> 00:57:04.610
That's why I deserted.

00:57:06.220 --> 00:57:08.020
Knowing that you could face the firing squad?

00:57:08.020 --> 00:57:11.520
I can deal with that more easily than killing.

00:57:11.520 --> 00:57:14.390
Then why did you enlist?

00:57:14.390 --> 00:57:16.760
Why did you give your signature?

00:57:17.260 --> 00:57:20.430
You weren't forced to! You did it
of your own volition, right?

00:57:21.900 --> 00:57:22.940
Well?!

00:57:22.940 --> 00:57:26.000
I was stupid too.

00:57:26.000 --> 00:57:29.010
I was just trying to act cool and show off.

00:57:29.010 --> 00:57:31.810
I had dreams of living the cool-guy life,

00:57:31.810 --> 00:57:34.550
so I left Japan, and I signed on as soon
as I was offered the chance.

00:57:34.550 --> 00:57:39.780
I thought I'd be assigned to a remote
border patrol unit or something.

00:57:40.320 --> 00:57:44.550
I figured what the heck. It seemed
kinda like a romantic adventure.

00:57:45.660 --> 00:57:47.290
And look what happened...

00:57:47.290 --> 00:57:49.190
Only half a year of training,

00:57:49.190 --> 00:57:51.820
then I'll get sent to the frontlines!

00:57:52.360 --> 00:57:54.500
At that moment, I realized something
for the first time.

00:57:54.500 --> 00:57:56.870
This ain't Shibuya or Harajuku.

00:57:56.870 --> 00:57:58.600
As soon as you leave the tourist resort town,

00:57:58.600 --> 00:58:01.040
you're in Aslan, with bullets
flying all over the place.

00:58:01.040 --> 00:58:02.210
If this were my own country,

00:58:02.210 --> 00:58:05.140
I'd have been able to pick up a gun for the
sake of my patriotism and my principles.

00:58:05.140 --> 00:58:07.110
But that's not how it is!

00:58:07.110 --> 00:58:08.480
It's all business here!

00:58:08.480 --> 00:58:09.750
"How much per head?"

00:58:09.750 --> 00:58:11.450
"How much per shootdown?"

00:58:11.450 --> 00:58:14.090
They told us to go to war because
they'd pay us for it!

00:58:14.090 --> 00:58:16.720
That's what you're doing, Mr. Kazama!

00:58:16.720 --> 00:58:18.020
Lemme tell you something...

00:58:18.020 --> 00:58:19.660
You're no patriotic soldier at all!

00:58:19.660 --> 00:58:21.830
You're a bloodthirsty cutthroat, who gets paid
under contract for all his killing!

00:58:21.830 --> 00:58:24.000
Yeah, you have a killer's eyes.

00:58:24.000 --> 00:58:26.330
It's not that I wanted to talk to you.

00:58:26.330 --> 00:58:27.870
I just had them call you here

00:58:27.870 --> 00:58:30.800
because I wanted to see the eyes of a Japanese
who's skilled at killing people.

00:58:31.470 --> 00:58:35.170
I don't think that I was wrong.

00:58:35.910 --> 00:58:40.710
To you I'm probably just a spineless
Japanese, but this is my...

00:58:40.710 --> 00:58:44.450
But this is how I'll take responsibility
for being so foolish and shallow.

00:58:44.450 --> 00:58:45.650
I mean...

00:58:45.650 --> 00:58:47.750
surviving by killing other people...

00:58:47.750 --> 00:58:50.820
That's just not something we were
ever taught in Japan.

00:58:50.820 --> 00:58:53.090
Right? You know what I mean?

00:59:12.510 --> 00:59:14.180
STOP IT!

00:59:14.180 --> 00:59:16.550
PLEASE HELP ME!

00:59:20.290 --> 00:59:23.150
MOMMA!

00:59:54.820 --> 00:59:57.260
I knew you'd come.

00:59:57.260 --> 00:59:58.620
Mr. Kanzaki...

00:59:58.620 --> 01:00:00.690
Would you mind shutting the door?

01:00:00.690 --> 01:00:04.130
You see, I've been hounded by
the media since the incident.

01:00:04.130 --> 01:00:07.600
I've been doing my work like this,
holed up at a hotel.

01:00:07.600 --> 01:00:09.840
It looks like there's hope for a
good solution to our problem

01:00:09.840 --> 01:00:11.900
of guaranteeing compensation to
the bereaved families, but still...

01:00:11.900 --> 01:00:17.510
It seems that your loyal subordinate has been
underfoot lately trying to dig up dirt on me,

01:00:17.510 --> 01:00:20.510
and I'm sure you wouldn't want to be
caught here either, now would you?

01:00:20.510 --> 01:00:22.880
Mr. Kanzaki, I'd like to try
asking you once more...

01:00:22.880 --> 01:00:23.850
Give it a rest.

01:00:23.850 --> 01:00:27.950
The terms I gave are no different than what
I told you on the phone this afternoon.

01:00:27.950 --> 01:00:30.960
I need money too, now more than ever.

01:00:30.960 --> 01:00:34.630
I simply cannot purchase your stock
at the rate you want.

01:00:34.630 --> 01:00:37.330
However, seeing as this is such
a desperate request for you,

01:00:37.330 --> 01:00:39.630
I've agreed to help out under certain conditions.

01:00:40.230 --> 01:00:43.940
So, you said that you could bear
anything for Kazama's sake.

01:00:43.940 --> 01:00:46.200
Now you can prove that.

01:00:52.940 --> 01:00:55.780
It must have been pretty humid out there.

01:00:55.780 --> 01:00:58.510
Feel free to take a shower first, if you like.

01:01:01.890 --> 01:01:06.190
You're not a child, you know.
You should know what to do.

01:01:06.190 --> 01:01:09.390
I mean... You were prepared for this when
you came here, weren't you?

01:01:14.170 --> 01:01:17.970
If you aren't ready, then by all
means feel free to leave.

01:01:17.970 --> 01:01:20.630
I understand how you feel.

01:01:21.610 --> 01:01:24.780
You talk about oh, how you love him and
oh, how you believe in him,

01:01:24.780 --> 01:01:27.950
but what it boils down to is that you
just don't want to get hurt.

01:01:27.950 --> 01:01:29.810
Well, I guess our deal is off then, isn't it?

01:01:29.810 --> 01:01:32.480
And Kazama won't get to come home.

01:02:05.550 --> 01:02:07.020
How about that, Shin?

01:02:07.020 --> 01:02:09.490
Ryoko's finally come to be with me!

01:02:09.490 --> 01:02:13.930
I am now going to trample over
what you value most of all!

01:02:57.940 --> 01:03:00.040
Who are you?

01:03:00.040 --> 01:03:02.410
What do you think you're doing?

01:03:06.110 --> 01:03:08.580
Shin...

01:03:09.250 --> 01:03:12.050
If I do this to help you...

01:03:12.480 --> 01:03:14.720
Will you be glad?

01:03:18.690 --> 01:03:20.750
No! Stay out!

01:03:25.230 --> 01:03:26.560
Miss Tsugumo!

01:03:27.430 --> 01:03:28.560
Ms. Yasuda?!

01:03:39.980 --> 01:03:41.480
Mr. Kanzaki,

01:03:41.480 --> 01:03:44.810
how dare you do such a thing to the daughter of
Mr. Tsugumo, to whom you owe so much?!

01:03:46.620 --> 01:03:49.820
You little rat... I'm impressed you were
able to sniff me out here.

01:03:49.820 --> 01:03:52.690
Mr. Kanzaki, a warrant for your
arrest has been issued

01:03:52.690 --> 01:03:54.790
under suspicion of misappropriation
of corporate funds, bribery,

01:03:54.890 --> 01:03:57.620
forgery of private documents and
use of those documents.

01:03:57.730 --> 01:03:59.790
Would you please come along with me?

01:04:12.010 --> 01:04:15.340
So are the fireworks over?

01:05:22.580 --> 01:05:27.580
What?! The rebel forces have launched
an attack on the capital?!

01:05:28.190 --> 01:05:31.350
So my father's finally set foot upon
this holy land after all?

01:05:34.430 --> 01:05:37.300
Attention all Area 88 personnel!

01:05:37.300 --> 01:05:40.570
The rebel forces have made their move
and are attacking the Aslan capital.

01:05:40.570 --> 01:05:44.300
Presently, the capital's defense
forces are returning fire,

01:05:44.300 --> 01:05:48.610
but the government army is at
an extreme disadvantage.

01:05:48.610 --> 01:05:51.840
Therefore by my order as your commander,

01:05:51.840 --> 01:05:54.550
tight security measures will be
enforced throughout Area 88.

01:05:54.550 --> 01:05:58.250
All personnel assume combat stations and
remain on standby until further orders!

01:05:58.250 --> 01:06:00.990
Anyone who deserts under enemy fire
will be shot on sight!

01:06:00.990 --> 01:06:01.920
Hah!

01:06:01.920 --> 01:06:03.890
This sure turned into one hell of a mess.

01:06:03.890 --> 01:06:06.260
The roles have totally reversed!

01:06:06.260 --> 01:06:10.660
Hey, so if the government army loses,
what's gonna happen to us?

01:06:10.660 --> 01:06:13.160
We'll all be arrested as traitors.

01:06:13.160 --> 01:06:15.430
And then hung!

01:06:15.930 --> 01:06:18.270
It ain't like the war is over yet.

01:06:18.270 --> 01:06:21.800
There'll be plenty more chances to do
some killing in the skies here.

01:06:22.210 --> 01:06:24.470
Seems I'm not too well-liked.

01:06:24.740 --> 01:06:29.650
Does it really bother you that much
that I shot a pilot who ejected?

01:06:29.650 --> 01:06:33.080
The fact that we're killers remains
the same either way, you know.

01:06:33.080 --> 01:06:35.120
You really enjoy killing, don't you?

01:06:35.120 --> 01:06:36.220
Damn right I do.

01:06:36.220 --> 01:06:37.880
It's thrilling.

01:06:39.860 --> 01:06:42.790
Sooner or later, you'll come to understand too.

01:06:45.730 --> 01:06:47.130
Roundell is?

01:06:47.130 --> 01:06:48.970
They're requesting permission to land, Sir.

01:06:48.970 --> 01:06:50.800
Very well, turn on the runway lights!

01:07:05.320 --> 01:07:06.280
Enter.

01:07:09.390 --> 01:07:11.290
You wanted to speak with me?

01:07:16.390 --> 01:07:20.300
This is King Zak. I've brought him here
from the royal palace.

01:07:20.300 --> 01:07:23.200
He's just sleeping under sedation.

01:07:23.840 --> 01:07:25.900
The king is fleeing to France.

01:07:25.900 --> 01:07:27.410
I'd like you to fly escort.

01:07:27.410 --> 01:07:28.710
Escort?

01:07:28.710 --> 01:07:31.040
I have already made arrangements
with the French government.

01:07:31.040 --> 01:07:34.750
Fuel supply will be one problem,
so fly there via Swiss airspace.

01:07:34.750 --> 01:07:37.620
They are a neutral state, so you'll
encounter no trouble there.

01:07:37.620 --> 01:07:38.620
And...

01:07:38.620 --> 01:07:41.090
Japanese national, Shin Kazama:

01:07:41.090 --> 01:07:43.560
Upon entrusting the king to the custody
of the French government,

01:07:43.560 --> 01:07:45.390
you will thereby be dismissed from service.

01:07:46.660 --> 01:07:48.090
Shin...

01:07:48.090 --> 01:07:49.920
Go home to Japan.

01:07:50.460 --> 01:07:51.930
Saki!

01:08:01.270 --> 01:08:03.570
Two years and five months...

01:08:05.910 --> 01:08:07.350
It was such a long time.

01:08:07.350 --> 01:08:10.750
I'd help carry your bags, but you
don't really have any.

01:08:10.750 --> 01:08:14.450
Well, I had nothing but the shirt on my back
when I was brought here after all.

01:08:23.390 --> 01:08:28.260
You better forget all about Area 88 right away
once you're back in Japan.

01:08:28.630 --> 01:08:32.400
If you get hung up on this crap,
you'll end up just like me.

01:08:34.040 --> 01:08:35.710
I owe you.

01:08:35.710 --> 01:08:37.880
So I'm losing one of my best customers, am I?

01:08:37.880 --> 01:08:39.640
Stay well, old man.

01:08:49.350 --> 01:08:52.490
Leaving without saying bye to me?
Talk about cold...

01:08:52.490 --> 01:08:54.790
You sure as hell like to pick fights with me.

01:08:54.790 --> 01:08:56.120
Why is that?

01:08:57.700 --> 01:09:00.960
Probably 'cuz I'm Asian, just like you.

01:09:01.270 --> 01:09:03.400
Must be nice having a country
you can go back to.

01:09:03.400 --> 01:09:06.540
I hear Japan's a nice and peaceful
place to live, huh?

01:09:06.540 --> 01:09:08.570
Completely different from my own country.

01:09:08.570 --> 01:09:12.810
You know, I was torn from my mother's body just
after she'd been blasted in a bombing raid.

01:09:12.810 --> 01:09:15.910
Well, I guess I'm saying that the
place I was born was Hell.

01:09:15.910 --> 01:09:18.380
After that, I spent all my life
walking through that Hell,

01:09:18.380 --> 01:09:22.850
and then one day I realized I'd become someone
who couldn't be satisfied unless he saw blood.

01:09:22.850 --> 01:09:26.310
That's probably the difference
between you and me.

01:09:28.460 --> 01:09:33.160
Well, see ya. Now get lost. It's too bad
we couldn't become friends.

01:09:38.100 --> 01:09:39.470
Nguyen,

01:09:39.470 --> 01:09:42.170
how you kill people is entirely up to you,

01:09:42.170 --> 01:09:45.540
but shredding a flesh-and-blood opponent
with your 20mm cannon

01:09:45.540 --> 01:09:47.210
isn't worth the cost of ammo.

01:09:49.250 --> 01:09:50.680
True enough!

01:09:50.680 --> 01:09:53.710
Thanks, I'll try and keep that in mind.

01:09:57.090 --> 01:10:00.360
Shin, nice work these past
two years and five months.

01:10:00.360 --> 01:10:03.390
Please take good care of my uncle, the king.

01:10:03.390 --> 01:10:06.860
Saki, what is going to become of Aslan now?

01:10:06.860 --> 01:10:11.360
What does it matter? I thought it didn't
have anything to do with you.

01:10:17.110 --> 01:10:20.980
Saying goodbye isn't easy for any of them.
They're a sentimental bunch.

01:10:24.150 --> 01:10:27.690
Control tower to zero-zero section,
Shin Kazama.

01:10:27.690 --> 01:10:29.120
Take off!

01:11:16.470 --> 01:11:18.730
Okay, put out the runway lights.

01:11:18.970 --> 01:11:20.670
Commander Saki! It's blue section!

01:11:20.670 --> 01:11:21.730
What?!

01:11:26.940 --> 01:11:30.510
Saki, we're going out for a little bit,
just to see Shin to the border.

01:11:40.790 --> 01:11:43.260
'Cuz he'll never make it as far as Switzerland

01:11:43.260 --> 01:11:46.490
if he starts any dogfights before
reaching Aslan's border.

01:11:49.870 --> 01:11:51.770
Those guys...

01:11:56.070 --> 01:11:57.410
Look, don't worry!

01:11:57.410 --> 01:12:00.440
We'll be back once Shin has made it
safely across the border.

01:12:00.880 --> 01:12:04.110
We're not deserting under enemy fire,
so don't you shoot at us!

01:12:14.760 --> 01:12:15.990
I give up!

01:12:15.990 --> 01:12:20.260
They may look tough, but they're
a bunch of softies inside.

01:13:51.220 --> 01:13:53.690
We'll be in Paris very soon, won't we?

01:13:53.690 --> 01:13:57.330
I'm sure your father will be at the airport,
eagerly waiting for you.

01:13:57.330 --> 01:14:02.200
I wonder if he's completed the 300 million yen
bank transfer with the Aslan government?

01:14:02.200 --> 01:14:06.500
It will be all right. I made sure to remind
him just before we left Japan.

01:14:06.500 --> 01:14:11.530
We're so fortunate that someone turned up to
purchase the stocks with legitimate funds.

01:14:15.480 --> 01:14:18.570
Just a little bit longer and
I'll be able to see Shin.

01:14:29.860 --> 01:14:31.430
Welcome, King Zak.

01:14:31.430 --> 01:14:35.090
The French government shall see to it
that you are kept safe.

01:14:41.070 --> 01:14:43.840
Japanese national, Shin Kazama...

01:14:43.840 --> 01:14:48.470
You are relieved from duty in the Aslan
Foreign Legion from this day forth.

01:14:49.210 --> 01:14:51.720
You are a free man now.

01:14:51.720 --> 01:14:54.150
Here's your passport,

01:14:54.150 --> 01:14:57.590
as well as your wages earned
in the Foreign Legion.

01:14:57.590 --> 01:14:59.820
They have been converted into US dollars.

01:14:59.820 --> 01:15:01.550
Thank you.

01:15:02.030 --> 01:15:04.930
And about your Tigershark...
What will you do with it?

01:15:04.930 --> 01:15:06.360
If you intend to sell it,

01:15:06.360 --> 01:15:09.330
I'd be willing to negotiate with the
Air Force on your behalf.

01:15:11.070 --> 01:15:13.070
I'll let you handle it then, thank you.

01:15:13.070 --> 01:15:16.240
Very well! I will contact you when we
have reached an agreement.

01:15:16.240 --> 01:15:19.230
When you've decided upon a hotel,
please let me know its address.

01:15:34.130 --> 01:15:38.090
I am now... free at last!

01:15:39.560 --> 01:15:41.170
Ryoko!

01:15:41.170 --> 01:15:43.530
Father!

01:15:45.000 --> 01:15:46.900
Are you feeling better now?

01:15:46.900 --> 01:15:50.340
Yeah, I'm finally able to get out
and about like this.

01:15:50.340 --> 01:15:54.910
So, Father, did you make the payment
at the National Bank?

01:15:54.910 --> 01:15:56.780
Listen, about that, Ryoko...

01:15:56.780 --> 01:16:00.250
The fighting in Aslan's civil war
has reached the capital now,

01:16:00.250 --> 01:16:03.090
and so the banks have suspended
all transactions.

01:16:03.090 --> 01:16:04.120
What?!

01:16:04.120 --> 01:16:07.560
I inquired at the embassy, but it was no use.

01:16:07.560 --> 01:16:11.630
They say they're too busy evacuating tourists
and foreign residents to worry about this.

01:16:11.630 --> 01:16:13.660
Then what about Shin?!

01:16:14.200 --> 01:16:19.340
Will the government suppress the rebel forces?
Or will a new government be formed?

01:16:19.340 --> 01:16:22.270
We'll hear what happened to him
only after that's been decided.

01:16:22.940 --> 01:16:24.600
Miss Tsugumo!

01:17:04.220 --> 01:17:06.680
Please cheer up, Miss Tsugumo.

01:17:06.680 --> 01:17:08.290
If necessary,

01:17:08.290 --> 01:17:11.460
I'll go to the embassy every day and maintain
close contact with them about the situation!

01:17:11.460 --> 01:17:12.960
That's right, Ryoko.

01:17:12.960 --> 01:17:16.660
You've come far already. You must not
give up hope until the very end!

01:17:48.190 --> 01:17:51.000
Why don't we go out for some dinner together,
since it's been so long?

01:17:51.000 --> 01:17:52.730
Come on now, don't be so upset!

01:17:52.730 --> 01:17:57.290
And just as a distraction, why don't we go do
some sightseeing in town after dinner?

01:18:29.600 --> 01:18:31.500
I'm thirsty.

01:18:39.640 --> 01:18:42.940
What could it be, this thirst?

01:18:45.920 --> 01:18:50.080
I feel it even though I've come back
to a world that's at peace.

01:18:50.820 --> 01:18:52.480
Lovers...

01:18:52.990 --> 01:18:54.690
Families...

01:18:55.490 --> 01:19:00.160
There's neither fear of air raids nor
the smell of gun smoke here.

01:19:00.160 --> 01:19:02.630
There won't be any mission briefings
this evening.

01:19:02.630 --> 01:19:04.600
There won't be any full-scale
offensive tomorrow.

01:19:04.600 --> 01:19:06.400
It's peaceful.

01:19:06.400 --> 01:19:10.000
So why am I feeling so damned irritated?

01:19:10.240 --> 01:19:11.710
Why is my heart thirsting?

01:19:11.710 --> 01:19:15.170
Hey, bro, whatcha doing sittin'
there talking to yourself?

01:19:15.610 --> 01:19:18.980
Don't tell me you're looking around
for a hotel, are you?

01:19:18.980 --> 01:19:22.350
If you are, you want me to show you
a great place that's cheap too?

01:19:30.860 --> 01:19:32.360
Haven't we come far enough?

01:19:32.360 --> 01:19:35.460
I don't exactly think you plan to
show me to any hotels.

01:19:35.800 --> 01:19:37.640
If there's something you want with me,
then hurry up and get it done now.

01:19:37.640 --> 01:19:40.200
After all, I do need to find someplace
to stay tonight.

01:19:40.200 --> 01:19:42.230
I don't have the time to hang
around with you kids.

01:19:42.810 --> 01:19:44.600
Now you're askin' for it!

01:19:46.880 --> 01:19:48.650
Whoa, the bastard grinned!

01:19:48.650 --> 01:19:50.550
Hey, man, this guy's givin' me the creeps!

01:19:51.120 --> 01:19:53.140
He's obviously just bluffing! Ya idiot!

01:20:17.040 --> 01:20:19.210
What the hell is this guy?!

01:20:19.210 --> 01:20:20.910
He's a frickin' monster!

01:20:35.730 --> 01:20:37.090
<i>Ye s?</i>

01:20:38.100 --> 01:20:40.160
What? The police?

01:20:40.160 --> 01:20:42.330
Very well, put me through.

01:20:44.900 --> 01:20:47.870
Yes, the passport is a perfect match,

01:20:47.870 --> 01:20:51.600
but when he said to call you and see,
I thought he was full of it, so...

01:20:52.840 --> 01:20:55.040
Huh? Foreign legion?!

01:21:05.220 --> 01:21:08.460
Your sponsor has come for you.

01:21:08.460 --> 01:21:10.730
But I think you're bad news.

01:21:10.730 --> 01:21:15.470
You may have been an ace fighter pilot
in a foreign legion, but this is Paris.

01:21:15.470 --> 01:21:17.770
So maybe killing men on the battlefield
makes you a hero,

01:21:17.770 --> 01:21:20.700
but in this world it'll only get you
charged with homicide.

01:21:21.510 --> 01:21:24.510
Well, this didn't turn out to be a murder case,

01:21:24.510 --> 01:21:26.910
and those men he subdued were
on our most wanted list,

01:21:26.910 --> 01:21:28.910
which ought to earn him public honors.

01:21:28.910 --> 01:21:31.580
But well, it just wouldn't look good after all.

01:21:31.580 --> 01:21:35.690
What we mean is that when you escorted
King Zak as he fled Aslan,

01:21:35.690 --> 01:21:37.720
it was all off the records, see?

01:21:37.720 --> 01:21:40.060
There would be a lot of trouble if
this is leaked to the public.

01:21:40.060 --> 01:21:41.490
You get it, right?

01:21:41.490 --> 01:21:47.160
If the media catches wind of this, it's sure to
damage our country's reputation.

01:21:48.100 --> 01:21:51.770
Would you mind getting out of the
country as soon as possible?

01:21:51.770 --> 01:21:53.100
It's not just you.

01:21:53.100 --> 01:21:56.940
Former soldiers always cause trouble
one way or another.

01:21:57.510 --> 01:22:00.840
If you're going back to Japan, I'll
take care of all the formalities.

01:22:02.480 --> 01:22:04.480
Aren't you going back to Japan?

01:22:04.480 --> 01:22:06.970
Then will you go to Switzerland? Or the US?

01:22:10.050 --> 01:22:12.920
Then where in the world do you want to go?

01:22:19.630 --> 01:22:22.470
Have you found a buyer for my Tigershark?

01:22:22.470 --> 01:22:26.200
No, I haven't been in touch with the military yet.

01:22:27.600 --> 01:22:29.240
Then please fuel it up.

01:22:29.240 --> 01:22:30.640
The external fuel tank too.

01:22:30.640 --> 01:22:31.780
I'll pay you for it.

01:22:31.780 --> 01:22:34.800
Now, hold on! Just where do you mean to go?

01:22:40.080 --> 01:22:41.550
Aslan...

01:22:41.550 --> 01:22:43.050
That's absurd!

01:22:43.050 --> 01:22:45.460
That country is right on the verge of
undergoing a regime change!

01:22:45.460 --> 01:22:48.660
All that will be waiting for you
there is the gallows!

01:22:48.660 --> 01:22:50.690
My comrades are there.

01:22:50.690 --> 01:22:53.530
They're a good bunch of guys.

01:22:53.530 --> 01:22:55.300
I wonder why it is?

01:22:55.300 --> 01:22:58.770
Being back in civilian life,
I feel this thirst in my heart.

01:22:58.770 --> 01:23:01.710
Even if I go walking around town,
or go eat at a restaurant,

01:23:01.710 --> 01:23:04.140
I don't feel uplifted in the least.

01:23:04.140 --> 01:23:07.340
Everyone seems so transparent.

01:23:07.340 --> 01:23:09.210
I wonder why that is?

01:23:09.210 --> 01:23:12.920
Even though I finally came back to the free
world I longed for so much,

01:23:12.920 --> 01:23:17.350
it was as though I'm wandering around
in the midst of some mirage.

01:23:17.990 --> 01:23:20.220
I guess when I got into it with those three hoods,

01:23:20.220 --> 01:23:23.390
that was about the only thing
I got any amusement out of.

01:23:24.390 --> 01:23:26.600
How did I ever get these kinds of feelings?

01:23:26.600 --> 01:23:29.070
I don't even understand it myself!

01:23:46.420 --> 01:23:49.750
Oh! Sorry, but would you mind
pulling over a moment?

01:23:53.560 --> 01:23:55.190
What's the matter?

01:23:55.190 --> 01:23:58.900
Well, there is someone I'm really indebted to,
who's in Paris now.

01:23:58.900 --> 01:24:00.860
I tried to call him several times,

01:24:00.860 --> 01:24:03.630
but it looks as if I may have
gotten the wrong number.

01:24:04.070 --> 01:24:07.530
Well, the guy who looked it up for me
was a loony old codger after all.

01:24:26.720 --> 01:24:29.490
Tsugumo residence. Ms. Yasuda?

01:24:29.490 --> 01:24:32.900
Hello? Why are you calling so late?

01:24:33.460 --> 01:24:34.870
Ryo...

01:24:34.870 --> 01:24:36.560
Ryoko, is it you?

01:24:37.200 --> 01:24:40.040
Shin... It is you, isn't it, Shin?

01:24:40.040 --> 01:24:43.370
Ryoko... So you've come to Paris?

01:24:43.370 --> 01:24:46.780
You're okay, aren't you, Shin?
And you're in Paris too, right?!

01:24:46.780 --> 01:24:49.010
Where are you now? Can you come here?

01:24:49.010 --> 01:24:51.010
I'll come to pick you up, okay?!

01:24:51.010 --> 01:24:53.080
Tell me where you're calling from.

01:24:53.080 --> 01:24:55.750
Oh, Shin, there are so many things
I want to talk about!

01:24:55.750 --> 01:24:57.020
My father's doing fine, by the way.

01:24:57.020 --> 01:24:58.860
He's already made a complete turnaround!

01:24:58.860 --> 01:25:01.160
And Ms. Yasuda's here too!
Do you remember Ms. Yasuda?

01:25:01.160 --> 01:25:01.920
She's that...

01:25:02.690 --> 01:25:04.060
Shin...

01:25:07.000 --> 01:25:08.090
Shin!

01:25:08.570 --> 01:25:09.860
Shin!

01:25:10.800 --> 01:25:11.960
Ryoko?!

01:25:20.980 --> 01:25:22.470
Shin!

01:26:22.240 --> 01:26:24.940
Large enemy aircraft formation approaching!

01:26:24.940 --> 01:26:27.740
Repeat, large enemy aircraft
formation approaching!

01:26:27.740 --> 01:26:30.710
All right, here the bastards come!

01:26:31.380 --> 01:26:32.880
Saki!

01:26:32.880 --> 01:26:36.850
Before we sortie out, there is something
I'd like to share with you men.

01:26:36.850 --> 01:26:39.220
Why you being so formal?

01:26:39.220 --> 01:26:43.130
After you've taken off, cut straight
through their formation.

01:26:43.130 --> 01:26:46.160
There will be no need to reverse
and engage in any dogfights.

01:26:46.160 --> 01:26:47.530
What did you say?

01:26:47.530 --> 01:26:49.230
Once you have escaped the combat zone,

01:26:49.230 --> 01:26:52.740
keep on flying flying towards your homelands,
as far as your fuel will take you.

01:26:52.740 --> 01:26:55.470
As of now, every one of you is
discharged from service!

01:26:55.470 --> 01:26:57.500
Aw, man! Are you sayin' we're fired?!

01:26:58.110 --> 01:26:59.780
Once you men have made your sortie,

01:26:59.780 --> 01:27:04.380
Area 88 will likely raise the white flag
in an unconditional surrender.

01:27:04.380 --> 01:27:09.820
This is the Aslan government's decision,
and perhaps its last.

01:27:09.820 --> 01:27:13.760
Because a new government will most likely
be formed as early as tonight.

01:27:13.760 --> 01:27:16.330
Roundell, after the foreign legion has sortied

01:27:16.330 --> 01:27:19.560
notify the ground crew and
administrative staff of this.

01:27:19.560 --> 01:27:23.190
And the job of flying the white flag
shall be yours.

01:27:23.600 --> 01:27:26.230
Lieutenant Colonel! What about you?

01:27:27.200 --> 01:27:31.510
If a new government is formed,
I will be tried for treason.

01:27:31.510 --> 01:27:34.310
I am not doing this as a Lieutenant Colonel
of the Royal Aslan Air Force,

01:27:34.310 --> 01:27:37.750
but rather as the commander of
Area 88's foreign legion,

01:27:37.750 --> 01:27:40.120
because in that capacity I must see
that my troops escape to safety.

01:27:40.120 --> 01:27:45.420
And I know there's a whole bunch of people here
who'd like to watch me go down.

01:27:46.360 --> 01:27:47.720
Damn straight!

01:27:47.720 --> 01:27:50.330
C'mon, you unemployed bastards! Let's go!

01:27:50.330 --> 01:27:51.560
Right on!

01:28:08.040 --> 01:28:09.510
It's sad...

01:28:09.850 --> 01:28:14.510
I doubt the day will ever come when that
man no longer smells of gunsmoke.

01:28:39.610 --> 01:28:41.810
Well? Is it a relief or what?

01:28:42.250 --> 01:28:43.880
The sound of the engine that you can
feel in your belly?

01:28:43.880 --> 01:28:45.680
The smell of slightly dirty oil?

01:28:45.680 --> 01:28:48.020
The cockpit that's more cramped than a coffin?

01:28:48.020 --> 01:28:51.590
Those are the only things that'll
quench your thirsting heart.

01:28:51.590 --> 01:28:53.420
You're wrong.

01:28:53.420 --> 01:28:55.660
The hell he is!

01:28:55.660 --> 01:28:58.400
Going back to civilian life should
have made it clear to you.

01:28:58.400 --> 01:29:01.900
Whoever stains his hands with blood will never
be able to lead a respectable life again,

01:29:01.900 --> 01:29:03.430
no matter how hard he tries.

01:29:03.430 --> 01:29:05.400
We are killers.

01:29:05.400 --> 01:29:08.460
You can make whatever excuses you like,
but it won't change that fact.

01:29:08.810 --> 01:29:13.010
Those who have fallen into Hell can
only seek out a purpose there.

01:29:13.010 --> 01:29:15.750
And they drift farther and farther
from civilian life.

01:29:15.750 --> 01:29:16.610
You're wrong!

01:29:16.610 --> 01:29:18.350
I ain't wrong!

01:29:18.350 --> 01:29:22.820
You're the same as me. That's why I said what
I did, that I thought we'd get along well.

01:29:22.820 --> 01:29:24.790
No! No, you're wrong!

01:29:25.290 --> 01:29:27.260
You see, I figured it out.

01:29:27.260 --> 01:29:30.560
I realized that the source of my
obsession is Area 88!

01:29:34.000 --> 01:29:36.000
That's why I'll go back.

01:29:36.000 --> 01:29:37.630
To rid myself of this obsession!

01:29:43.810 --> 01:29:45.570
Here they are...

01:29:47.880 --> 01:29:50.750
Now listen up. I don't want to see
any hotdogging up here.

01:29:50.750 --> 01:29:52.680
All you need to do is fly straight
through their line.

01:30:27.450 --> 01:30:29.210
You fools! Don't turn around!

01:30:29.750 --> 01:30:31.090
Ain't no helping it!

01:30:31.090 --> 01:30:34.820
If we just say goodbye like this,
we'll never get to see you go down!

01:30:34.820 --> 01:30:38.160
At this point, even if you do come along,
you'll receive no payment!

01:30:38.800 --> 01:30:39.960
Don't need it!

01:30:39.960 --> 01:30:44.200
There's no one who'd dig a grave for a bunch of
guys who are just looking for a place to die!

01:30:44.200 --> 01:30:47.830
No fool's gonna bring a dowry with him
on his trip to Hell!

01:30:48.940 --> 01:30:50.310
You bastards...

01:30:50.310 --> 01:30:52.940
Me, I've never been to the next world,

01:30:52.940 --> 01:30:55.970
so I'm countin' on you to show us the way, Saki!

01:30:56.250 --> 01:30:59.680
All right, you idiots who can't even
calculate profit and loss...

01:30:59.680 --> 01:31:00.450
Follow me!

01:31:39.090 --> 01:31:40.920
Damn! I can't shake 'em.

01:31:46.700 --> 01:31:48.260
Damn! Not now!

01:32:18.430 --> 01:32:19.430
Damn!

01:32:19.430 --> 01:32:21.090
Guess I wasted too much ammo.

01:32:29.510 --> 01:32:31.740
Saki! How many of us left?

01:32:31.740 --> 01:32:33.680
Maybe six or so?

01:32:34.010 --> 01:32:36.340
Mickey, about how much ammo
do you have left?

01:32:36.980 --> 01:32:39.780
Another three or four seconds'
worth and I'm dry.

01:32:39.780 --> 01:32:42.340
Good enough... Want to make another pass?

01:32:55.530 --> 01:32:57.300
Bearing 120.

01:32:59.870 --> 01:33:01.390
Altitude 19,000.

01:33:04.140 --> 01:33:05.840
Speed 1,400 knots.

01:33:14.020 --> 01:33:16.110
The course is all clear!

01:33:17.390 --> 01:33:18.480
GO!

01:33:56.060 --> 01:33:59.230
So long, my love

01:33:59.230 --> 01:34:03.130
Naiteru hito yo
<i>Oh, weeping woman</i>

01:34:03.130 --> 01:34:08.660
Douka wasurete
<i>Please try to forget</i>

01:34:10.470 --> 01:34:17.280
Futari no mabushii tsukihi
<i>Those brilliant days when we were together</i>

01:34:17.280 --> 01:34:25.020
Ai no natsu wo
<i>That summer of love</i>

01:34:25.020 --> 01:34:32.160
Ikiteru kanashimi mo shirazu ni
<i>The days you were innocently in love</i>

01:34:32.160 --> 01:34:38.500
Mujaki ni koi shita hi
<i>Without even knowing the sadness of living</i>

01:34:39.170 --> 01:34:46.610
<i>I can see your blurry image</i>
Sora no screen kimi ga nijinderu

01:34:46.610 --> 01:34:53.020
<i>On the screen in the sky</i>
Sora no screen kimi ga nijinderu

01:34:57.490 --> 01:35:07.490
Kokoro wa kinou e kaere to yuu kedo
<i>My heart tells me to go back to yesterday</i>

01:35:11.830 --> 01:35:19.110
<i>But my body starts running</i>
Karada wa hitori ni yoake e kakedasu

01:35:19.110 --> 01:35:26.240
<i>Towards the dawn on its own</i>
Karada wa hitori ni yoake e kakedasu
